 demand spike of 135 arrives together with a product-0 order. Candidate 7's smaller final orders win back only about 280. So candidates 7, 5 and 1 rank below candidate 6.\n\n**Candidate 3** orders daily at about 1.1×. That means 27 order days at 36 each (972) against 14 for candidate 6 (504), so 468 more in fees. Daily deliveries save only about 240 in storage. They also lose the cushion a two-day delivery gives: a high-demand day can draw on the next day's share. Overall it comes out about 200–250 worse than candidate 6.\n\n**Candidate 0** orders every three days at about 1.1×.\n- It saves 180 in fees, but carrying the larger deliveries costs about 225 more in storage.\n- It sits close to the 300-unit limit more often: product 1 arrives the day after product 0, when about two thirds of the product-0 delivery is still on hand.\n- It caps the order for the demand spike (190 against about 272 needed), which means a shortfall of roughly 40 units on days 18–20.\n\nThe net result is a little worse than candidate 6."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 358, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5807, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 358}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T02:03:24.648Z", "request_id": "req_011CgAmieYc4LaCjowMpxbuu"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Qv4yAFbeUBaPtrFzjQJATf", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "